{%- comment -%}
  /collections — every collection the store publishes. Brief §5 puts
  "Collections" in the main navigation next to Shop.

  This route used to render main-stub. The distinction the brief draws between
  the two entries is the one this theme now implements: Shop is the whole
  catalogue with a filter rail over it, Collections is the way in by category —
  the same destination reached by choosing rather than by narrowing.

  THESE LINKS DELIBERATELY DO NOT CARRY THE IN-STOCK FILTER, and every other
  entry point into the catalogue does. The difference is what the reader just
  did. `filter.v.availability=1` is on /collections/all because a bare catalogue
  opened on a wall of sold-out cards nobody asked for — 106 of the 126 products
  on this store are sold out, which is real data from the studio's own Shopee
  listing. But choosing a collection IS the narrowing; hiding that category's
  sold-out pieces on top of it answers a question the reader did not ask.

  It was also a tile that lied. The count below is the whole collection, so a
  filtered link made the tile say "4 pieces" and open on "No pieces match these
  filters" — which is what the store's first real collection did, `test`, all
  four of its products sold out. Either the number follows the link or the link
  follows the number; this section keeps the number, because the number is the
  fact about the collection and the filter was the thing added on top.

  The photograph falls back from the collection's own image to its first
  product's shot to the labelled placeholder — the same three-step the category
  mosaic uses, so a collection needs no art direction of its own to look
  deliberate. Most of this catalogue has no photography yet, so most tiles draw
  the placeholder at final size.

  THE COUNT IS `all_products_count`, NOT the filtered size. It answers "how big
  is this collection", which is a fact about the collection; counting only the
  in-stock ones would shrink it as stock moves and would read as the category
  itself getting smaller. With the filter off the link, it now matches what the
  tile opens. Storefront filter counts are computed against the filtered set and
  there is no whole-catalogue equivalent — the same platform limit
  catalogue-filters.liquid records.

  Collections with nothing in them are skipped. An empty collection is a
  configuration state, not a category, and a tile promising a category the store
  cannot show is the dead link this repo refuses.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg">
  <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">
    {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'page heading' %}
  </h1>

  {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
    <p class="mt-5 wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
  <ul class="mt-block grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {%- for list_collection in collections -%}
      {%- if list_collection.all_products_count == 0 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}

      {%- liquid
        assign tile_image = list_collection.image
        if tile_image == blank
          assign tile_image = list_collection.products.first.featured_image
        endif
      -%}

      <li data-reveal>
        <a href="{{ list_collection.url }}" class="group flex flex-col gap-4">
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
            {% render 'media',
              image: tile_image,
              ratio: '4 / 5',
              sizes: '(min-width: 1024px) 30vw, (min-width: 640px) 46vw, 92vw',
              label: 'Collection photo',
              class: 'rounded-none transition-transform duration-(--duration-base) motion-safe:group-hover:scale-[1.03]' %}
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-h3 leading-h3 text-ink transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) group-hover:text-brand">
              {{ list_collection.title }}
            </h2>
            <span class="shrink-0 text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
              {{ list_collection.all_products_count }} {{ 'catalogue.pieces' | t: count: list_collection.all_products_count }}
            </span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>

  {%- if shown == 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      No collections defined yet, which is where this store is until the category
      collections are created in the admin. The alert names the state rather than
      drawing placeholder tiles: an empty /collections is a configuration gap the
      studio can close, not a layout waiting on photography.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign none_yet = 'collections.none' | t -%}
    <div class="mt-7">{% render 'alert', tone: 'info', body: none_yet %}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collections",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Collections" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Intro" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
